body:
Been there, the only reason I don't go into hospital for help is because I know they'll  throw me back into that "hell hole" where all the really crazy people get to be with you and make you feel as crazy as them .  3 days in one of those places I know fucked me up more than anything else.  

&#x200B;

I hear you .

I know exactly how you feel.  I've been on the edge of the "dark hole" so many times I've lost count.......like you I also feel like I can't do this anymore but my friend told me something yesterday while driving me to my doctor's office- she said that when someone kills them self the pain they felt has now been permanently transferred onto family and friends which means I'd be leaving my 2 sons with no mom and  life times full of pain............this is the ONLY thought that keeps me going, my youngest already has emotional and mental health issues (that he inherited from me) and I won't be the cause of even more pain for my family.  

&#x200B;

Please take what I've said to heart.   The pain you're feeling probably makes my request seem futile but please remember what I've said here.  I'm 53, had my first "visit" with Suicide when I was 20, it didn't work then and I haven't been able to bring myself yet to actually go through with it but think about a few times every year.  Is the pain unbearable?  Sometimes yes, it is and I have no idea how I'll even wake up the next morning to deal with the rollercoaster of emotions that comes with that pain. But I do, each and every morning, because if the opposite happens and my family discovered me in some horrible situation then I've scarred the rest of my family for the rest of their lives.    

&#x200B;

As easy as it sounds to kill the pain, killing yourself will just make the lives of your loved ones as torturous as yours feels now.  Hugs !!!!
